WEBVTT

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:29.300
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:29.300
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:29.300
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.350 --> 00:02:02.850
Chapter VII

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.700
On October 9th,
Space Year 788...

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:17.800
...funeral rites for Admiral Alfred Rosas, retired, of the Free Planets Alliance were observed.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.700
Though the military sponsored it, the
ceremony was carried out at his home...

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.850
...at the insistence of the only bereaved, his granddaughter, Miriam Rosas.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.020
The last of the 730 Mafia has
left the face of the earth.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.160
It's the end of an era.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.520
An accidental
overdose of sleeping pills ?{He mistook the amount
of sleeping pills ?}

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.060
As they say, the bed is closer to
death than the battlefield is.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.700
At least he didn't die in pain,
so it was better in that sense.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:54.730
But why on earth could none of
the 730 Mafia die of old age ?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.830
Hey...

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.250
Lt. Commander Yang.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.170
Um...my...sincere condolences...

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.740
Miss Rosas...

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.150
You may call me Miriam.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.680
Do you talk to your
girlfriend that way, too ?

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.290
"Miss So and So" ?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.800
I don't have a girlfriend.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.170
That was a pathetic thing to say.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.560
And it's even more pathetic
because it's actually true.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.810
It's a ceremonious
funeral, isn't it ?

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.710
Ah, is it appropriate to say
"ceremonious" to describe a funeral ?

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:45.460
Not one-tenth of the people
here are actually grieving.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.340
They are only here
as a formality.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.260
Even if it's just one-tenth, that's
still a significant number of people.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:55.600
Besides, even if they aren't actually grieving,
at least they're probably having regrets.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.740
And is that the
case with you ?

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.870
Yes.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:02.650
I believe I respected
Admiral Rosas very much.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:09.000
I'm not good with people of grand status,
but I wish I had met your grandfather earlier.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.470
Thank you.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.700
If my grandfather had known that,
he would have been pleased.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.870
Grandfather was fond of you.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.050
I was surprised because
it was so sudden.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.600
I was told it
was an accident ?

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.990
He was unfortunate.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.510
Bruce Ashbey takes his colleagues'
fortunes away even after his death.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.100
No one among the 730 Mafia
died as boldly as they lived.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.670
What's wrong ?

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.650
Is there something
you want to say ?

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.200
Miss Rosas...

00:04:52.200 --> 00:05:00.340
...I'd like to respect your feelings, but what 
you say might offend the deceased admirals.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.860
Well, I mean,
this is what I think.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:11.390
Each of the 730 Mafia Admirals were heroes in their own lives...

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:15.450
...and none of them
were believers in Fate...

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.750
Lt. Commander Yang, aren't
you confusing fact with truth ?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.400
Fact and truth ?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.050
That the members
of the 730 Mafia...

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:32.600
...found meaning and fulfillment in
their own lives is a truth for them.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:41.260
But as an objective fact, if their legitimate rights
are being violated, it is unfair to let that continue.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.870
That's...

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.230
I might be being meddlesome,
but she's got a point.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:53.930
If I say, "Everyone was happy, so what's wrong
with it ?" then there's no point in studying history.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:01.500
Admiral Rosas's rights were infringed upon, is what you think, isn't it ?

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.200
My grandfather's too, I mean.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.400
My grandfather often assumed the
duty of Bruce Ashbey's staff officer...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.700
...but of course, I'm not talking about the general notion that...

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.700
..."a staff officer's accomplishments are his commander's accomplishment."

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.860
That's not the kind of
thing I'm trying to say.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.230
This woman is like
a goddess of words.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.050
Is there any
concrete evidence ?

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:29.260
"You should investigate
it yourself," right ?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.150
Miss...

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.390
Miriam, what are you
planning to do now ?

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.760
Um...I might be
being nosy here, but...

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.810
You sure are being nosy.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.700
I'm sorry.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.050
You're needlessly
apologizing, again.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.420
You don't have to worry.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.510
I have a legitimate fiancé.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.240
He's on Phezzan now, so he couldn't come to the funeral.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.580
He's 15 years older than I am, 
and he's an engineer on a merchant ship.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.700
He's not particularly
talented or handsome...

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:22.830
...but my grandfather liked him because he's conscientious and sincere.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.380
Yes, that's...

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:28.150
To congratulate her
would sound stupid...

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.810
...and it's probably not 
appropriate in a place like this...

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.260
By the way,
Lt. Commander Yang.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.980
Are you going to keep investigating the
case of Bruce Ashbey's supposed murder ?

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.160
Do you think you can
catch the murderer ?

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.300
I'm not a military policeman, so...

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:49.270
So I didn't plan on outing
the culprit from the start.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.390
What I wanted to do
was something else...

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:58.020
I never intended to
find the culprit, so...

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.650
It doesn't sound
like sour grapes.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.180
No, that is sour
grapes, I think.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.780
Well, goodbye,
Lt. Commander Yang Wenli.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:24.050
I hope you'll be able to garner
accolades without hurting other people.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.050
What happened ?

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:45.320
You look like a cat that
let a bird get away.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.600
What's that supposed to mean ?

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.010
In the end, was it
actually an accident ?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.090
It's not certain whether it
was an accident or suicide.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.940
But it does seem to have been decided
that no foul play has taken place.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:02.030
The police are not making
the details available.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.680
Who is that man ?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:16.250
That conspicuous man who
looks like a stage actor ?

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.100
Huh ?

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.470
That's Job Truniht.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.540
He's the most famous among
the young congressmen.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.940
He just became a member of the
National Defense Committee, I think.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:33.350
It's rumored he'll be a Cabinet
member in two or three years.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:37.000
As a rising stock, he's
in the same boat as you.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.230
As far as I'm concerned, I don't
care if anyone buys my stock.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.650
It's been a long time.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.650
Hey, Attenborough.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.940
You're so dedicated to come here.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.650
It's a military funeral.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.550
All students at the military
academy were brought out here.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.560
Though I don't mean
they're here reluctantly.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:03.080
Admiral Rosas was a
distinguished person.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.200
And more importantly, it's nice
to have classes cancelled.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.290
You haven't changed - 
you still say things in poor taste.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.700
Don't make too much
trouble, all right ?

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.050
You're graduating 
next year, aren't you ?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:19.590
This is good timing.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.440
If you have some time,
why don't you come with us ?

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:23.700
If you're going to
pick up the tab...

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.990
The person in charge
of the wallet is here.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:26.990
Hey !

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.780
That's the story...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.560
...but what do you
think, Attenborough ?

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.800
That sounds silly.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:51.950
Silly ?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.500
I mean, if we'd killed
Admiral Ashbey like that...

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.670
...who was going to protect us
from the hands of the Empire ?

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.950
To kill Admiral Ashbey...

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.600
...would be like digging
a hole under your feet.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:13.480
You're right, but there are many
precedents like this in history.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.940
Cases where a power-holder kills
an influential military commander...

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.050
...out of his own self-interest
and untrusting nature.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:29.300
In many cases, it leads to the collapse of the nation, but there are many other cases...

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:33.450
...where those influential
commanders seized power.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:37.200
In other words, nations
collapse in either case.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:43.600
Even if you block one path to destruction,
there comes another path to destruction.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.560
That's right, I guess.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.350
Just as humans die,
nations die in the end.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.130
The difference is whether they
live a long or short time.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:57.750
In any case, you still haven't found out
who sent those letters, Senior Yang ?

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:00.980
So far, I haven't a clue.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:02.090
"So far" ?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.550
It could be just
as well, but...

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.180
Truths are always
plural, aren't they ?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.160
Huh ?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.150
The truth of the ones
who fight the war...

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.530
...the truth of the ones who order others to fight the war...

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:21.300
...and the truth of the ones who are made to fight the war.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.370
Each of those is different.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:29.550
How about hearing from nameless
soldiers about Admiral Ashbey ?

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:32.800
Of course, there are
many voices of discontent.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:36.220
But "Thousands die to
raise one hero to fame."

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.950
That's the truth
of human society.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.050
We can't just
blame Admiral Ashbey.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.670
I have no intention of blaming him.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.680
I don't have that right.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:50.430
You don't have to
force a conclusion.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:54.780
Even if you come to a conclusion,
it doesn't mean that it'll be made public.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:58.700
Then why am I doing this ?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.000
To learn about life.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:16.770
In any case, let's drink to Admiral Rosas and the 730 Mafia, for today.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:29.950
After the death of Bruce Ashbey,
the 730 Mafia became powerless.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.950
Following the
2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.390
...they were separated and none
of them became the leader of a clique.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:42.600
Baron Wallice Warwick continued to fight
the Empire as a frontline commander.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.560
In Space Year 749,
he was promoted to Admiral...

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.200
...and in Space Year 751, he was
appointed to be Space Fleet Chief Commander.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:53.700
Afterwards, there were no
major battles for two years...

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.990
...and in 753, he retired
from the force, unscathed.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:58.490
He was only 43 years old.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:04.990
After a year's hiatus, he served as
president of a famous private university.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:10.130
After three years of eventless presidency,
he turned to politics in his birthplace, Palace...

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:13.080
...and served four years
before moving to the capital.

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:18.300
In 760, he became the National Defense
Committee Chair in the Supreme Congress...

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:23.220
...and at the same time, he was given the title of Fleet Admiral for his past contributions.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:27.960
He was also popular in social circles,
and though it seemed like a fairy-tale life...

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:31.130
...he was surrounded by scandals.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.050
Though he himself was never
involved in any crime...

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:39.550
...graft was uncovered in his National Defense Committee and it involved a suicide case.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:42.700
As a result, he had to leave his
position in the aftermath of the scandal.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.300
Moreover, his lover of 5 years
died of a drug overdose...

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.520
...and with the addition of other smaller
incidents, Baron's popularity collapsed.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:54.300
He withdrew from both the
political world and social circles...

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:59.710
...and retired to a small town on
Heinessen along with his modest assets.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:05.060
In 766, he died of a heart
attack, at the age of 56.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:12.110
March Frederick Jasper remained in the
military the longest among the friends.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:17.730
In Space Year 749, he became an Admiral, and succeeding Baron Warwick...

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:21.830
...he was appointed to be Space Fleet Chief Commander in 753.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:26.560
Until he retired in 770, he fought against the Empire and stayed in the post for 17 years...

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:31.510
...which was the longest
tenure in said office.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:35.650
During that time, he received
the title of Fleet Admiral in 764.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:42.200
Between 770 and 771, he served as
the Head of the Joint Chiefs of Staff...

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.010
...but his performance
was merely average.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.650
He was truly a
man of the battlefield.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:53.150
After retiring in 771, he
went on vacation with his wife...

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:56.560
...but they both died
in a spaceship accident.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.560
He was 61 years old, and
his wife was 56 years old.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:04.300
In 750, John Drinker Cope
was promoted to Admiral...

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:07.040
...and became the Space
Fleet Sub-Commander...

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:13.030
...but died in the Battle of
Palantia in 751 at the age of 41.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.300
His strategic command
during this battle was...

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:20.660
...unlike his previous battles,
uninspired, and the loss was catastrophic.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.170
It was a debacle that
resulted in 300,000 casualties.

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:32.050
At that time, March Jasper led the rescue fleet to Palantia Starzone, but was 4 hours late.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:37.370
When he arrived, the Imperial fleet had already finished the battle and was on their way home.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:41.050
Jasper attacked them from behind and dealt some measure of revenge for the death of his friend.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:44.160
At least, that was his intention, but a cruel rumor circulated.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:48.830
The rumor was that Jasper could have made it in time if he wanted to, but didn't...

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:53.440
...because he wanted to monopolize the
battlefield accolades and left Cope high and dry.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:59.610
In grief over her husband's death, Mrs. Cope believed this rumor and denounced Jasper.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:03.660
Later, Mrs. Cope apologized to Jasper, but this incident, which left a bad taste with both parties...

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.290
...hurt both the living and the dead.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.500
When Cope received the title of Fleet Admiral after his death...

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:12.970
...Jasper reported it to the bereaved,
but avoided meeting Mrs. Cope.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:17.200
The Copes and Jaspers
never met again afterwards.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:23.980
The serious and calm Fang Tchew-ling was also promoted to Admiral in 750...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.500
...but did not seem particularly pleased and was composed as always...

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:31.030
...the same as he always was when entering a battlefield or other times.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:33.200
He became the Space
Fleet Sub-Commander...

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:35.050
...and then bypassed Space
Fleet Chief Commander...

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.940
...and ascended to a position on the Joint Chiefs of Staff in 755.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:41.700
He occupied that
post until 761...

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:46.860
...in tandem with the then-Space Fleet
Chief Commander, Jasper, for 6 years.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:51.740
There was no problem between the two in public, but they had no private relationship...

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:55.050
...and never even visited
each other's residence.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:02.200
In 761, after being given the title of Fleet Admiral, he retired from the military.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:06.640
He was said to have been a capable Head of the Joint Chiefs, with solid administrative accomplishments...

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:13.810
...and rational, though not
warm, personnel decisions.

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:16.080
He had poor luck in
his family circumstances.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:20.290
Since he had divorced his wife, and his
son had passed away, he led a lonely life.

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:23.080
After his retirement, he was given several honorary positions...

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.930
...but claiming that he would antagonize the younger officers if he worked hard...

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:29.920
...he spent his time alone,
feeding pigeons at the park.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:34.040
When he was 63 years old,
he suffered a lung embolism...

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.480
...and after two acute
incidents, he passed away.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.810
Even on the verge of death,
he was calm and apathetic.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:42.780
Does it hurt ?

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.650
Of course it hurts.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.720
My consciousness
is getting murky.

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:54.640
If I continue to speak, I'll probably say
nothing but nonsense, so I'll shut up.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.700
After saying those words...

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:02.300
...he kept quiet no matter what was
said to him, and died 40 minutes later.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:07.520
In his will, Fang Tchew-ling said that
neither a funeral nor burial was necessary.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.560
Though a funeral could be left
undone, a burial had to be done...

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:14.000
...so the burial was quietly carried out at a
cemetery in Corinth, by Rosas' arrangement.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:19.600
On his simple gravestone, the words engraved along with his name and dates, were...

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:22.500
..."Fang Tchew-ling's life
was worthy of our trust."

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:27.560
Upon Fang's death, Rosas lost all 
of his battlefield friends of the past...

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:34.700
...and lived a quiet and solitary life as the
last of the 730 Mafia for the next 15 years.

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:43.400
Was Admiral Rosas happy,
to have outlived his friends ?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:54.170
There is no reason that all the contemporaries of Ashbey must love, admire, and understand him.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:20:01.770
If I replace "Ashbey" with "Yang Wenli,"
those words could be a reality lesson for me.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:07.250
I could never be understood by everyone, and there is no need to lament it.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:11.100
I don't need to be so affected as to claim that solitude is the essence of my life...

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.270
...but I have to remember that
true friends aren't many.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:23.070
Computer, among those who participated in the
2nd Battle of Tiamat list those still in active service.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.590
As of October 12th,
from the 2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:32.930
...20 commanders, 20 officers and 35
soldiers, still remain in active service.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:35.720
Huh ?

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:38.400
Alexandor Bucock ?

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.760
I think I've heard
that name somewhere.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.080
Oh, just as I thought.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.660
He's the author
of this memoir.

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:55.250
He was 19 years old at
the time, which means now...

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.300
...he's 62 years old.

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.300
I see, he's now a Commodore.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:06.450
Wow, he's the police commander
of Marovia{lbier} Starzone ?

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.220
That's so far out
on the frontier.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.740
I guess I can't meet
him in person to talk.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.600
Have you finished reading Legends of
the Heroes of the Free Planets Alliance...

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.610
...Lt. Commander Yang ?

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:21.410
Your new assignment
has been decided.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:23.300
Eh ?

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:27.650
You're being assigned to the
POW Camp on Planet Econia.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:32.640
It came down suddenly, but you're expected to
depart Heinessen by the end of this month.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:37.250
A POW camp, huh ?

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.700
I'm not the superintendent yet, am I ?

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:43.960
You're Number 3.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.600
Superintendent, Vice-Superintendent, and then Secretary.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.110
The Superintendent is a Captain, the
Vice-Superintendent is a Commander...

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:52.110
...and the Secretary and Chief
Security Officer are Lt. Commanders.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:54.860
What does the Secretary do ?

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:58.490
When the Superintendent botches
something, you take responsibility for it.

00:21:58.490 --> 00:22:01.700
Then I'll just hope that the
Superintendent is competent.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:03.960
I guess you'll have to.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.320
Anyway, how long do you think
you'll have to stay there ?

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:11.000
Let's see, I guess I won't be able to return for at least one year.

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:14.040
Make it six months.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.890
Be patient for
that length of time.

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:17.900
I'll try my best to make arrangements so you can come back here by then.

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:20.890
I'll count on you.

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:25.540
Of course, that is as long as I don't get transferred somewhere myself.

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:30.530
Is this possibly because of my
investigation into Admiral Ashbey ?

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:31.890
I don't know.

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:36.530
In that case, perhaps...

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:40.160
Speculation is futile in this case.

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:41.700
You'll have to find
something more fruitful to do.

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:45.870
You can go home today,
so you can start packing.

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:46.750
Oh, well...

00:22:49.740 --> 00:22:54.160
Thus, Yang Wenli was to
depart Heinessen all of a sudden.

00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:58.520
What sort of intentions are
behind this unexpected assignment ?

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:02.010
Yang couldn't help
but speculate.

